{
  "A single-line text input with a label, help text and error display. It supports a placeholder, a prefix and suffix, buttons inside the box, a clear button, a password reveal button, a character counter, an input mask and validation, either on its own, in a group, or across all fields in a panel.": "",
  "Every prop accepts a value or a function, and a function that reads a reactive object keeps the field in sync with it. `x-model` provides two-way binding for the value. When you create the component with `new`, set the same properties programmatically.": "",
  "The label can appear above the box, next to it (`side`), inside it until there is a value (`floating`), or only for screen readers (`hidden`). `&` marks its access key.": "",
  "Prefix, suffix, icon and buttons": "",
  "`prefix` and `suffix` add fixed text around the value, and `icon` appears at the start. `buttons` adds custom buttons, each with its own `enabled`, `visible` and `position`.": "",
  "Password and character counter": "",
  "Input mask": "",
  "A mask keeps the text in the required format as the user types, deletes or pastes, and the caret skips fixed characters. The value contains only the typed characters, or the displayed text with `maskValue=\"formatted\"`. An incomplete mask fails validation.": "",
  "Character": "Karakter",
  "A digit.": "Bir rakam.",
  "An optional digit.": "",
  "A letter.": "Bir harf.",
  "A letter or a digit.": "Bir harf ya da rakam.",
  "Treats the next character as fixed: `\\\\0` is a fixed zero.": "",
  "A fixed character, skipped during typing.": "",
  "Validation": "Validation",
  "A field validates itself when it loses focus after a change, and then on every change until the value is valid. `required`, `minLength`, `type=\"email\"` and a mask bring their own rules, and `rules` adds your own, including asynchronous ones. `error` displays a message from an external source, such as the server.": "",
  "Without a group, `validateFields(panel)` validates every field inside a component or element, such as a panel, a dialog or a page.": "",
  "Commits the value (with `updateOn=\"change\"`) and raises `onEnter`.": "",
  "Custom buttons and the password button are Tab stops. The clear button is not, because Escape does the same thing.": "",
  "A native `<input>` associated with its `<label>` through `for`.": "",
  "`aria-invalid=\"true\"`. The message is a polite live region, so new errors are announced.": "",
  "The clear and password buttons get their names from `uiLocale`, and the password button has `aria-pressed`.": "",
  "The names of the clear and password buttons and all validation messages come from `uiLocale.strings`. Every field updates immediately when they change, including errors already on screen.": "",
  "The field. `data-size`, `data-variant`, `data-label-mode`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-filled`, `data-required`, `data-stretch`.": "Field. `data-size`, `data-variant`, `data-label-mode`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-filled`, `data-required`, `data-stretch`.",
  "Added by TextBox.": "TextBox'ın eklediği.",
  "The label, the box and the input.": "",
  "The parts on either side of the input.": "",
  "The width when the field is not stretched.": "",
  "Units: the box, a state layer over its fill, the frame (with `frame-start`, `frame-notch` and `frame-end` around a notch), the line along the bottom, and a ring for keyboard focus. Each has a box per state: by variant (`filled-…`, `underline-…`), by status (`invalid`, `readonly`, `disabled`), and for `hover`, `focus` and `pressed`.": "",
  "Units: the label (`focus`, `invalid`, `disabled`, `floating-…`), the required indicator and the parts next to the text.": "",
  "Units: button groups in the box, the buttons (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`) and their contents.": "",
  "Units: the line below the box (`shown`, `invalid`, `disabled`), the help or error text, and the counter.": "",
  "Frame width, spacing and the label.": "",
  "Icons, and the distance between the buttons and the edges of the box.": "",
  "The floating label and the notch cut for it.": "Yüzen label ve onun için kesilen çentik.",
  "The text. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "`top`, `side` (next to the box), `floating` (inside the box until there is a value) or `hidden` (for screen readers only).": "",
  "Help text shown below the box. An error message replaces it.": "",
  "`text`, `password`, `email`, `search`, `tel` or `url`. `email` and `url` also validate the format.": "",
  "Fixed text before or after the value inside the box (`https://`, `kg`).": "",
  "An icon at the start of the box.": "Kutunun başında bir icon.",
  "Custom buttons inside the box, at the start or end.": "",
  "With `type=\"password\"`, shows a button that reveals the password.": "",
  "Length limits. `minLength` is enforced by validation.": "",
  "Shows `12/50` below the box (`12` without `maxLength`).": "",
  "With `change`, the value updates when the field loses focus or the user presses Enter.": "",
  "The value can be read, selected and copied, but not changed.": "",
  "Adds an indicator after the label, `aria-required` and a `required` rule.": "",
  "See Input mask.": "",
  "Custom mask characters.": "",
  "Shown in positions that are not filled yet.": "",
  "`raw` returns only the typed characters, and `formatted` includes the fixed ones.": "",
  "With `focus`, an empty mask appears only while the field has focus.": "",
  "See Validation.": "Validation bölümüne bakın.",
  "An error from an external source, such as the server. It stays until cleared.": "",
  "The group the field is validated with.": "",
  "Accepts a value or a function, the same as the prop: `box.error = () => this.model.nameError` is tracked.": "",
  "`false` while an error is displayed.": "",
  "The error being displayed, or `''` if there is none.": "",
  "Indicates that an asynchronous rule is running.": "",
  "Indicates that every position of the mask is filled.": "",
  "Your `buttons` can be plain or reactive, and the field reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. Every editor has this method, and list editors also re-read their items.": "",
  "Occurs when the value changes. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`. `byUser` distinguishes user input from programmatic changes.": "",
  "Validators": "",
  "A value is required.": "",
  "An email address or a web address.": "",
  "A `RegExp`, or a string that must match the whole value, like the HTML `pattern` attribute.": "",
  "The number of characters.": "Karakter sayısı.",
  "A number or date within a range.": "",
  "Equal to another value, such as a repeated password, or different from it with `not`.": "",
  "`check(value)` returns `true`, `false`, a message, or a promise of one of these, such as a server call.": "",
  "`message` (a value or a function) and `enabled`. Empty values pass every rule except `required` and `compare`.": "",
  "The frame (`Field`), the mask (`InputMask`, which works on any `<input>`) and validation (`ValidationGroup`, `validateFields`, `checkRules`) are shared parts, exported for use in other components and your own code.": ""
}
